From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] FT: Fragment the FTE in the Reassociation Response frame when it exceeds 255 octets

With the MLO GTK, MLO IGTK, and MLO BIGTK subelements of two or more
links (about 110 octets per link) the FTE of the Reassociation Response
frame for a non-AP MLD exceeds the maximum element size. The Length
field was silently truncated, so the frame was malformed and the
non-AP MLD rejected every multi-link FT reassociation (it then retried
with a single link and re-associated shortly afterwards to get its
other links back).

Split the FTE into the element with 255 octets of data followed by
Fragment elements, as allowed since IEEE Std 802.11-2020 (10.28.11) and
already parsed by wpa_ft_parse_ies(). The MIC is calculated over the
FTE and the Fragment elements as they appear in the frame, including
the Fragment element headers, which matches the receiver side.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
@@ -2988,6 +2988,54 @@
 	ftie_len = res;
 	pos += res;
 
+	if (ftie_len > 2 + 255) {
+		/*
+		 * The FTE exceeds the maximum element size (e.g., with the MLO
+		 * GTK/IGTK/BIGTK subelements of several links), so it has to be
+		 * split into the FTE with 255 octets of data followed by
+		 * Fragment elements (IEEE Std 802.11, 10.28.11). The MIC is
+		 * calculated over the FTE and the Fragment elements as they
+		 * appear in the frame, i.e., including the Fragment element
+		 * headers, which is how wpa_ft_parse_ies() reconstructs the
+		 * protected data on the receiving side.
+		 */
+		size_t data_len = ftie_len - 2, rem, n;
+		size_t frag_len = 2 + 255 +
+			((data_len - 255 + 254) / 255) * 2 + (data_len - 255);
+		u8 *tmp, *src;
+
+		if (frag_len > (size_t) (end - ftie)) {
+			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+				   "FT: Not enough room for a fragmented FTE");
+			return NULL;
+		}
+		tmp = os_memdup(ftie + 2, data_len);
+		if (!tmp)
+			return NULL;
+		pos = ftie;
+		src = tmp;
+		*pos++ = WLAN_EID_FAST_BSS_TRANSITION;
+		*pos++ = 255;
+		os_memcpy(pos, src, 255);
+		pos += 255;
+		src += 255;
+		rem = data_len - 255;
+		while (rem > 0) {
+			n = rem > 255 ? 255 : rem;
+			*pos++ = WLAN_EID_FRAGMENT;
+			*pos++ = n;
+			os_memcpy(pos, src, n);
+			pos += n;
+			src += n;
+			rem -= n;
+		}
+		os_free(tmp);
+		ftie_len = pos - ftie;
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "FT: FTE fragmented: %u octets of data in %u octets of elements",
+			   (unsigned int) data_len, (unsigned int) ftie_len);
+	}
+
 	if (sm->wpa_key_mgmt == WPA_KEY_MGMT_FT_SAE_EXT_KEY &&
 	    key_len == SHA512_MAC_LEN) {
 		struct rsn_ftie_sha512 *_ftie =
